# Files that break, rather than merely look odd, if they arrive with CRLF.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto`, because that would renormalise the whole
# repository in one commit and bury real changes. Only the paths where a carriage
# return changes behaviour are pinned.
#
# The AUR is the sharp case. `.SRCINFO` is compared byte-for-byte against a fresh
# `makepkg --printsrcinfo` in CI, and a PKGBUILD with CRLF fails on Arch in ways
# that read as a packaging bug rather than a line-ending one. This repository is
# developed on Windows, where git hands the working copy CRLF by default, so
# without this the correctness of these files depends on each contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting.
packaging/aur/.SRCINFO  text eol=lf
packaging/aur/PKGBUILD  text eol=lf
*.sh                    text eol=lf

# Rasterised brand assets and the share card: binary, never touched by eol rules.
*.png                   binary
*.woff2                 binary
